# Committed on purpose (see .gitignore) -- this is just the public
# production API host, not a secret. Vite loads .env.production
# automatically for any `vite build` (Vercel prod AND preview deploys
# both build in Vite's "production" mode by default), so the app always
# has a working API base URL even if Vercel's dashboard env var is
# unset, misconfigured, or scoped to the wrong environment.
#
# Local dev is unaffected: `npm run dev` runs in Vite's "development"
# mode, which reads .env.local (see .env.local.example) instead.
#
# To point a build at a different backend temporarily, use
# .env.production.local (gitignored, takes precedence over this file) --
# don't edit this file for a one-off override.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://when-where.onrender.com
